id: pm-jhkzk0
title: Allow safe transaction previews in managed-package workspaces with derived dependency links
description: "A real pm item mutate --from intake.json --dry-run in this repository refuses transaction_preview_non_regular_file because installed extensions contain node_modules SDK links. The no-follow safety boundary and typed refusal are already delivered by pm-preview-path-refusal and pm-fa9olc; this is a distinct usability extension, not a claim those completed fixes are missing. Specify and implement a derived-package dependency exclusion or another safe preview source, without following links or ignoring authoritative tracker content."
type: Feature
status: open
priority: 2
tags[4]: agent-ux,packages,preview,sdk
created_at: "2026-10-25T16:47:02.100Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-25T17:51:18.072Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: "A managed-package tracker can preview item-only mutations without following dependency symlinks; authoritative non-regular entries still refuse; source bytes remain untouched; SDK, CLI and MCP share the contract; isolated fixtures cover managed dependency links and hostile authoritative paths."
parent: pm-9rgaal
risk: medium
confidence: medium
expected_result: "Normal package-managed tracker previews are useful and safe, with explicit classification of excluded derived dependencies and unchanged no-follow guarantees."
